 "operation": [
  {
   "topic": "Construction and marking",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Molded epoxy DO-41 body whose compound is rated UL 94 V-0. A coloured band marks the cathode end. Leads are matte tin plated, solderable to J-STD-002 and JESD 22-B102; the E3 suffix passes the JESD 201 class 1A whisker test and marks the RoHS-compliant commercial grade base part."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Soldering",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "Solder dip up to 275 °C for 10 s maximum, per JESD 22-B106."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Uses",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "General rectification in power supplies, inverters and converters, and as a freewheeling diode."
  },
  {
   "topic": "Ratings that depend on mounting",
   "page": 1,
   "text": "The 1.0 A average current and the 30 µA full-load reverse current are rated with 0.375 in (9.5 mm) of lead between body and mount, at 75 °C ambient and 75 °C lead respectively. Current derates linearly from 1.0 A at 75 °C ambient to zero at 150 °C."
  }
 ],
